Z||000002||Cheever2||07-19-2001||10:39 AM||||I finally got signed up on the Fiero-List email group to inform them of the Parts Relay.  In less than 12 hours I got 4 new members!  Now I need to add them to the website.<P>Anyway, I hope everybody will get accustomed to checking this list when they need something shipped, especially if the cost will be high.  It just might help.  We still need lots more volunteers in the Western US, and Canada too.<BR><P>------------------<BR>- <I>Chuck Hodges</I> -<BR><A HREF="http://home.houston.rr.com/fieropartsrelay" TARGET=_blank> Fiero Parts Relay</A> administrator||||reg||1
Z||000003||Two88GTs||07-20-2001||10:38 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 88CoupeV6:<BR><B>I just saw yours today. It will be there soon. I loaded it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> looks like new too. <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thanks, man!  It arrived Thursday damage-free despite having just bubble wrap and packing tape instead of having it boxed.  The previous owner of my 68k car put an aftermarket cat but apparently used mild steel extensions and one of the mild steel extensions developed a bad exhaust leak to the point that I was able to rip out the exhaust system in two pieces where the rust hole was.  Took me 3 hours to rip out the old exhaust out and put the new one in using a regular socket set and lots of Liquid Wrench.<BR>I just need to install all the exhaust springs tomorrow morning and voila!  No more exhaust leak!||||reg||1
